.TH THEME 6
.SH NAME
theme \- the toolkit's look, as a file
.SH DESCRIPTION
A theme file names the metrics and colours
.IR mui (2)
lays out and paints controls with, a role and a value per line:
.IP
.EX
role   value
.EE
.PP
.B #
starts a comment that runs to the end of a line, and a blank line is
skipped.
A role this build does not know, or a value it cannot read, is skipped as
well rather than refused, so a file written for a later build still loads
what it recognises.
.PP
.IR Mui (2)'s
.B parse_theme
reads a file's text into a
.B Theme
that starts at the built-in default, so a file that names nothing changes
nothing, and one that names a role changes that role alone.
It touches no file itself: a caller reads a theme file's bytes and hands
them to
.BR parse_theme .
.PP
The metric roles, each a non-negative number of pixels:
.TP 12
.B pad
a group's inset from its own edge to its children
.TP
.B gap
the space left between two siblings
.TP
.B bevel
the thickness of a raised control's lit and dark edges
.TP
.B hpad
a button's inset from its edge to its text, left and right
.TP
.B vpad
a button's inset from its edge to its text, top and bottom
.TP
.B well
a field's recess around the text it holds
.PD
.PP
The colour roles:
.TP 12
.B ground
the window behind the gadgets
.TP
.B face
a raised control's face
.TP
.B face.lit
a raised control's top-left highlight
.TP
.B face.shade
a raised control's bottom-right shadow
.TP
.B text
the ink a label is drawn in
.PD
.PP
A colour's value is one of
.IR palette (2)'s
own names, lower case with an underscore where the name has a space, such
as
.B slate_deep
or
.BR amber_hot ,
or six hex digits,
.BR rrggbb ,
naming red, green and blue directly.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
# a theme: copper controls on a near-black ground
face        copper
face.lit    copper_lit
face.shade  copper_dark
ground      0e131a
bevel       3
.EE
.SH FILES
No file under this name is read automatically; nothing in this tree yet
opens a theme file at start.
A program that wants one reads it itself, the way
.IR intuition (4)
reads
.IR keys (6)
and
.IR workspaces (6),
and calls
.B parse_theme
on the bytes before it lays out its first window.
.SH SOURCE
.B sys/libmui/theme.odin
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR mui (2),
.IR chrome (2),
.IR palette (2),
.IR intuition (4)
.SH BUGS
No program in this tree reads a theme file yet; every window opens at the
built-in default look until one is written that does.
